  "question": {
    "text": "If $y=\\cos \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}+\\cos ^{-1} \\frac{x}{2}\\right)$, then $(x-y)^2+3 y^2$ is equal to _____."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & y=\\cos \\left(\\cos ^{-1} \\frac{1}{2}+\\cos ^{-1} \\frac{x}{2}\\right) \\\\ & y=\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{x}{2}-\\sqrt{1-\\frac{1}{4}} \\sqrt{1-\\frac{x^2}{4}} \\\\ & 4 y=x-\\sqrt{3} \\sqrt{4-x^2} \\\\ & 3\\left(4-x^2\\right)=x^2+16 y^2-8 x y \\\\ & 12-3 x^2=x^2+16 y^2-8 x y \\\\ & 4 x^2+16 y^2-8 x y=12 \\\\ & x^2+4 y^2-2 x y=3 \\\\ & x^2+y^2-2 x y-3 y^2=3 \\\\ & (x-y)^2+3 y^2=3\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}